Component Where Role <code>messaging-proxy</code> pod <code>personal-gateway</code> namespace Accepts structured API calls (<code>send_message</code>, <code>read_messages</code>) from OpenClaw. Validates, rate-limits, and logs Host-side daemon or Shortcuts endpoint Mac mini macOS Receives HTTP requests from the proxy (via NodePort/localhost). Interacts with Messages.app via AppleScript or Shortcuts. Credentials never leave the host NetworkPolicy K8s <code>messaging-proxy</code> can only talk to the host on one specific port. OpenClaw can only talk to <code>messaging-proxy</code> <p>API contract example:</p> <pre><code>POST /api/messages/send
{
  "to": "+1234567890",
  "body": "Running 10 minutes late",
  "confirmation_required": true
}

Response: { "status": "pending_confirmation", "confirmation_id": "abc123" }
</code></pre> <p>The proxy never sends the message directly — it returns a confirmation ID. OpenClaw must relay this to the user. Only after the user confirms does the proxy forward the request to the host.</p>
